# 11. Task Creation and Assignment — Complete Workflow

This is one of the most important modules.

When the administrator creates a task, the backend must:

1. Authenticate the administrator.
2. Validate the task details.
3. Validate the deadline.
4. Validate the selected employees.
5. Verify all assigned employees are active.
6. Determine SOLO or GROUP assignment.
7. Create exactly one task document.
8. Create one taskMembers document for every assigned employee.
9. Generate an audit event.
10. Generate an individual notification for each assigned employee.
11. Return the created task.

### Solo assignment

One task, one assigned employee, one taskMembers document.

### Group assignment

One task, multiple assigned employees, one taskMembers document per employee.

When an employee opens their dashboard, the newly assigned task must appear.

When the administrator opens the task details, all assigned employees and their individual progress must appear.

Do not duplicate tasks to simulate group assignments.

Do not allow one employee to see another employee's private information unnecessarily.

### Task editing

When the administrator changes:

- Task title.
- Description.
- Priority.
- Deadline.
- Department.
- Assignment.
- Task status or configuration.

Persist the update and ensure relevant employees receive updated task data.

When the deadline changes, future reminder eligibility must use the new deadline.

When an employee is removed from a group task, update the assignment relationship safely and preserve relevant historical records.

