# 26. Testing Requirements

Do not stop after connecting Firebase.

Test the complete application workflow.

### Test 1 — Administrator authentication

- Log in as administrator.
- Refresh browser.
- Confirm session restoration.
- Confirm admin-only pages are protected.

### Test 2 — Employee creation

- Create Employee A.
- Create Employee B.
- Verify Firebase Authentication accounts.
- Verify Firestore user profiles.
- Verify unique employee IDs.
- Verify employees appear in the admin interface.

### Test 3 — Employee authentication

- Log out as administrator.
- Log in as Employee A.
- Confirm correct employee dashboard.
- Refresh the browser.
- Confirm the session persists.
- Confirm Employee A cannot access admin endpoints.

### Test 4 — Solo task assignment

- Log in as administrator.
- Create a solo task.
- Assign it to Employee A.
- Log in as Employee A.
- Confirm the task appears.
- Refresh.
- Confirm it remains visible.

### Test 5 — Group task assignment

- Create one group task.
- Assign it to Employee A and Employee B.
- Verify only one shared task document exists.
- Verify two separate taskMembers documents exist.
- Confirm both employees see the task.

### Test 6 — Independent status updates

- Employee A changes their status.
- Confirm Employee B's status does not change.
- Confirm administrator sees Employee A's update.
- Refresh all sessions and verify persistence.

### Test 7 — Status requests

- Administrator sends a request to both employees.
- Employee A responds.
- Employee B responds later.
- Confirm both responses are independently stored.

### Test 8 — Queries

- Employee A raises a query.
- Administrator answers it.
- Employee A sees the answer after refresh.
- Confirm the query does not automatically complete the task.

### Test 9 — Group communication

- Employee A sends a message.
- Employee B sees the message.
- Administrator can view the conversation.
- Unassigned Employee C cannot access it.

### Test 10 — Submission and approval

- Employee A submits.
- Confirm Employee B remains unsubmitted.
- Administrator reviews Employee A's submission.
- Administrator requests revision.
- Employee A sees the revision request.
- Employee A resubmits.
- Administrator approves.
- Confirm the final state persists.

### Test 11 — Notifications

- Generate several application events.
- Confirm correct recipients receive notifications.
- Mark a notification as read.
- Refresh.
- Confirm read state persists.
- Confirm one employee cannot modify another employee's notifications.

### Test 12 — Deactivation

- Administrator deactivates Employee B.
- Confirm Employee B cannot access protected application features.
- Confirm existing historical task records remain intact.

### Test 13 — Cross-device synchronization

Open the application in two separate browser sessions.

Use one as administrator and the other as an employee.

Perform updates in one session.

Confirm the relevant changes appear in the other session through the implemented synchronization mechanism.

### Test 14 — Security

Attempt:
- Employee accessing admin endpoints.
- Employee changing another employee's status.
- Employee approving their own submission.
- Employee accessing unrelated tasks.
- Employee reading another employee's notifications.
- Unauthenticated API requests.
- Invalid task status transitions.

All unauthorized operations must be rejected.

